# Angel Engine — Stride Cloud Build Kit

This is a build-automation starter for creating a Windows build of the real Stride Game Studio source as the technical foundation for Angel Engine. It is NOT a precompiled engine and does not yet rebrand the editor.

## Important
- The official Stride repository is the source of truth: https://github.com/stride3d/stride
- Current upstream build instructions require Git with Git LFS, Visual Studio 2026, .NET 10 and C++ desktop build tools. The full toolchain is too large for a Windows PC with 2 GB RAM and less than 5 GB free disk.
- The workflow below uses a GitHub-hosted Windows runner. This does require a GitHub repository and GitHub Actions; it cannot run inside the APK Builder itself or in a Linux-only Colab session because Game Studio is a Windows desktop editor.
- The workflow is an initial automation attempt, not a guarantee that upstream master builds without changes. Inspect logs and adjust if upstream changes.
- Stride is open source under MIT, but check THIRD PARTY notices for components with separate terms. Preserve upstream notices when redistributing.

## Use
1. Create a new public repository named `angel-engine` on GitHub.
2. Upload this kit's contents to the repository root, preserving `.github/workflows`.
3. Open Actions → `Angel Engine - Build Stride Game Studio` → Run workflow.
4. When it completes, download the `angel-engine-stride-build-logs` artifact first. If the workflow successfully locates a build output, it also uploads `angel-engine-gamestudio`.
5. Do not distribute it as a renamed product until we have added Angel Engine branding and reviewed license notices.

## What this kit does
- Clones the official Stride repository with Git LFS on a Windows runner.
- Installs/uses Visual Studio Build Tools and .NET 10 where available on the runner.
- Attempts to build `Stride.GameStudio` from the upstream solution.
- Uploads logs and any detected GameStudio output for inspection.

## Next engineering phase
After a successful upstream build, make a maintained fork and apply a deliberate branding patch (name, icons, product metadata, splash screen) without deleting license notices. Then build and test a minimal 3D project before calling the result Angel Engine 0.1.
